<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title
      >{{ brand }}’s ${{ som }} market analysis: {{ num_rivals }} competitors,
      {{ key_finding }}</mj-title
    >
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#FFFFFF">
    <mj-wrapper css-class="main" padding="0">
      <adv-header />

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          Hi <strong>{{ first_name }} </strong>
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          I ran your
          <a href="https://amazon.{{ amazon_tld }}/dp/{{ client_asin }}">{{
            client_asin_title
          }}</a>
          (ASIN: {{ client_asin }}) through our competitive intelligence tool
          and wanted to share what surfaced.
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          The analysis identified
          <strong> {{ num_rivals }} direct competitors</strong> across your
          category. They are capturing
          <strong> ${{ som }} in monthly revenue.</strong>
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          {{#each market_analysis_summary}}
          <p class="paragraph" style="">{{{ . }}}</p>
          {{/each}}
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          {{#has_rivals

          }}<span style="display: inline-block" class="para-space">
            Below is a detailed analysis {{ ../num_top_rivals }} of your market
            rivals:</span
          >
          {{/has_rivals}}
        </mj-text>
      </para>
      <para>
        <mj-raw>
          {{#has_rivals}}
          <table style="width:100%; border-spacing: 0; border-radius: 16px;
          overflow: hidden; border:1px solid #D0D5DD !important; max-width:
          100%;" class="table-section"> <!-- Table Header --> <tr> <td
          class="header-cell" style="background-color: #f2f4f7; padding: 16px;
          width:18%; border-right: 1px solid #d0d5dd; vertical-align: bottom">
          <span class="revenue-header" style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;
          line-height: 24px; color: #088ab2">Rival &<br /> Rev/mo</span> </td>
          <td class="header-cell" style="padding: 16px; border-right: 1px solid
          #d0d5dd; background-color: #f2f4f7; width: 25%; vertical-align:
          bottom"> <span class="revenue-header" style="font-size: 16px;
          font-weight: 600; line-height: 24px; color: #088ab2">Their strength<br
          /> vs you</span> </td> <td class="header-cell last-cell"
          style="padding: 16px; background-color: #f2f4f7; width: 23%;
          vertical-align: bottom"> <span class="revenue-header"
          style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 24px; color:
          #088ab2">Your advantage<br /> vs them</span> </td> </tr> <!-- Table
          Rows -->
          {{#each ../competitors}}
          <tr> <td class="table-body-cell" style="padding: 16px;
          background-color: #ffffff; border-right: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
          border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; vertical-align: top"> <a
          class="competitor-name" href="https://amazon.{{ ../../amazon_tld

          }}/dp/{{ asin }}" target="_blank" style=" text-decoration: underline;
          font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; overflow: hidden; color: #088ab2;
          display: -webkit-inline-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 4; width: 18ch;
          text-overflow: ellipsis; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; ">
          {{ rival_title }}
          </a> <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #344054;
          font-weight: 600; margin-top: 8px !important; margin-left: 0;
          margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">${{ monthly_revenue }}/mo</p>
          </td> <td class="table-body-cell" style="padding: 16px;
          background-color: #ffffff; border-right: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
          border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; vertical-align: top"> <span
          class="revenue-amount" style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 300;
          color: #344054"> {{ strength_of_rival }} </span> </td> <td
          class="table-body-cell" style="padding: 16px; background-color:
          #ffffff; border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; vertical-align: top"> <span
          class="reason-text" style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 300; color:
          #344054"> {{ advantage_over_rival }} </span> </td> </tr>
          {{/each}}
          </table>
          {{/has_rivals}}
        </mj-raw>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          What you’re seeing above typically takes
          <strong
            >{{#has_rivals}}20–30{{/has_rivals

            }}{{^has_rivals}}several{{/has_rivals}} hours of weekly manual
            analyst work.</strong
          >
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>
          Our
          <strong
            ><span>Rev</span><span style="color: #088ab2">Up</span></strong
          >
          Engine automates this proactively by mapping full category revenue
          dynamics, review velocity, and competitive positioning signals. This
          is
          <strong
            >real competitive intelligence, not surface-level scraping.</strong
          >
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text
          ><strong>You’re already in our beta –</strong> I need your feedback on
          whether these are the right competitors to track, what insights matter
          most to you (price changes, ranking shifts, review velocity), and what
          actions you’d take with this intelligence.
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text
          ><strong
            >In the end, only two opinions matter: your customers’ and
            yours.</strong
          >
          We strive to provide you with the insights to achieve both, and we
          believe that together with your inputs we have a much higher chance of
          doing this for you. In exchange, I’ll show you:
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-raw>
          <ul style="padding-left: 26px; margin: 0;"> <li><strong>Revenue trend
          and seasonality</strong> across all tracked rivals so you can see
          who’s gaining/losing share MoM and plan inventory/pricing
          accordingly.</li> <li><strong>Review velocity tracking</strong> to
          surface momentum early—often before it shows up in rank—so you can
          respond with PDP upgrades or promos.</li> <li><strong>Positioning &
          keyword gap analysis</strong> to pinpoint where your skylight-specific
          value is invisible versus Prime/badge-led substitutes.</li> </ul>
        </mj-raw>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text
          ><strong>15 minutes, no pitch—just analysis and feedback.</strong>
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text>Best,<br />Anders </mj-text>
      </para>

      <para>
        <mj-text
          font-size="16px"
          color="#344054"
          font-weight="300"
          line-height="24px"
          padding="0 0 0 0"
          >P.S. We’re working with a select group of ~100 brands whose feedback
          shapes what we build. You’re one of them.
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <ai-button
        classes="meeting-btn btn-wrapper"
        href="https://revup{{ app_subdomain_suffix }}.amaizing.io/book-your-session?uuid={{uuid}}"
        >Let's meet!</ai-button
      >

      <para classes="button-link">
        <mj-text
          padding="0"
          font-size="12px"
          line-height="18px"
          color="#344054"
        >
          Button not working? https://revup{{
            app_subdomain_suffix
          }}.amaizing.io/book-your-session?uuid={{ uuid }}
        </mj-text>
      </para>

      <adv-footer />
    </mj-wrapper>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
